# 05. Entity Ownership

Each entity has one authoritative domain owner.

| Entity | Primary purpose |
|---|---|
| Observation | Raw observed information |
| Signal | Interpreted/structured signal from an observation source |
| Anomaly | Signal that requires attention |
| Event | Operational occurrence being tracked |
| Threat | Characterized or suspected threat context |
| RiskAssessment | Assessment of operational risk |
| Investigation | Structured examination of an event/threat |
| Case | Individual operational case |
| Finding | Evidence-backed investigative result |
| TransmissionAssessment | Assessment of possible transmission relationships |
| ContainmentAction | Intervention intended to limit spread/exposure |
| ResponseAction | Operational response activity |
| RecoveryAssessment | Assessment of stabilization/recovery |
| PreparednessLesson | Learning captured from an event |
| ResilienceGap | Identified weakness |
| ImprovementItem | Action intended to address a gap |
| ResearchFinding | External/internal research information |
| Location | Geographic/organizational location context |
| Actor | Person/system acting within AEGIS |
| Evidence | Supporting information |
| Notification | User-facing operational notification |
| AuditRecord | Historical accountability record |
| DomainEvent | Record of a meaningful state-changing occurrence |

