# 58. Real-Time Event Payload

Conceptually:

```text
{
  "eventId": "...",
  "eventType": "THREAT_STATUS_UPDATED",
  "entityType": "Threat",
  "entityId": "...",
  "occurredAt": "...",
  "version": 4,
  "data": {}
}
```

The production event envelope must be standardized before implementation.

---

# 59. Data Freshness

AEGIS must communicate data freshness when real-time accuracy matters.

Conceptually:

```text
LIVE
RECENT
STALE
UNKNOWN
OFFLINE
```

Freshness is separate from data correctness.

A stale dataset can still be historically correct.

---

# 60. Data Synchronization

The system should support:

```text
Initial Load
 ↓
Current State
 ↓
Incremental Updates
 ↓
Reconciliation
```

A client should not need to reload the entire application after every event.

---

# 61. Offline / Degraded Mode

If AEGIS supports degraded operation, the data architecture must distinguish:

```text
locally known state
```

from:

```text
authoritative server state
```

The UI must never falsely imply that an offline mutation has become authoritative unless the system explicitly supports and reconciles it.

---

# 62. Security Classification

Data sensitivity must be classified at the architecture level.

Potential conceptual categories:

```text
Public
Internal
Sensitive
Restricted
```

The final classification system must be determined by the deployment organization and applicable governance.

Do not invent a classification policy inside frontend code.

---

# 63. Data Minimization

AEGIS must only collect and retain information necessary for legitimate operational purposes.

Especially for patient-related information:

```text
minimum necessary
purpose limitation
access control
auditability
retention policy
```

must be enforced at the system level.

AEGIS should not become a general-purpose patient information warehouse.

---

# 64. Sensitive Data Separation

Where sensitive information is required, architecture should separate:

```text
operational metadata
```

from:

```text
sensitive subject information
```

This enables broader operational visibility while limiting unnecessary exposure.

---

# 65. Access Control

Access to an entity must depend on:

```text
Actor
+
Role
+
Organization
+
Permission
+
Context
```

not merely:

```text
isAdmin = true
```

The exact authorization model belongs in the security architecture.

---

