# 88. AI Coding Agent Data Rules

AI agents working on AEGIS must follow these rules:

### Rule 01

Never invent a new domain entity because a component needs one.

### Rule 02

Never invent a new status without checking the canonical state model.

### Rule 03

Never rename an existing field casually.

### Rule 04

Never change a domain relationship without updating the architecture.

### Rule 05

Never use local component state as operational truth.

### Rule 06

Never create fake API responses that contradict the canonical model.

### Rule 07

Never create unrelated mock entities.

### Rule 08

Never silently remove required fields.

### Rule 09

Never bypass authorization for convenience.

### Rule 10

Never represent uncertainty as certainty.

