# 95. Final AEGIS Data Principle

The entire data architecture can be reduced to one model:

```text
             EVIDENCE
                ↓
            KNOWLEDGE
                ↓
             ASSESSMENT
                ↓
              DECISION
                ↓
               ACTION
                ↓
              OUTCOME
                ↓
              LEARNING
                ↓
           PREPAREDNESS
                ↓
          FUTURE SIGNALS
```

AEGIS must preserve the distinction between every layer.

It must never turn:

```text
signal → threat
```

without appropriate interpretation.

It must never turn:

```text
threat → certainty
```

without evidence.

It must never turn:

```text
recommendation → action
```

without authorization.

It must never turn:

```text
action → success
```

without verification.

And it must never turn:

```text
history → forgotten state
```

merely because the current state changed.

That is the foundation of trustworthy AEGIS data architecture.

---

# 96. Master Data Contract

The final contract between the product, design, engineering, and AI systems is:

```text
ONE DOMAIN
      ↓
ONE CANONICAL DATA MODEL
      ↓
ONE STATE MODEL
      ↓
ONE CONTRACT
      ↓
MANY SCREENS
      ↓
MANY COMPONENTS
      ↓
MANY USERS
```

The interface may change.

The visualization may change.

The technology stack may change.

The database implementation may change.

But the **meaning of the operational data must remain coherent**.

AEGIS is not successful because it contains a beautiful dashboard.

AEGIS is successful when every visualization, interaction, decision, action, and learning loop can be traced back to trustworthy, structured, auditable data.
